<title>USA: Federal Signal positioned for '97 growth.</title>
<headline>Federal Signal positioned for '97 growth.</headline>
<dateline>OAK BROOK, Ill. 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Signal Corp president Joseph Ross Thursday described the company's 1997 performance outlook as &quot;very favorable.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Current order rates, expected new product introductions and the continuing benefits of cost reduction actions we have taken this year position us for an excellent 1997,&quot; Ross said in a statement.</p>
<p>Federal Signal manufactures signaling products, custom signage, consumable industrial tooling and environmental vehicles. The company on Thursday raised its quarterly dividend 15.5 percent to $0.1675 per share.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
